-- 0015 (SEED): reference data for public.intake_known_senders.
--
-- intake_known_senders is a GLOBAL directory of known email senders/brands (no org
-- scoping). It is the lookup table behind public.lookup_known_sender() (0013), which is
-- called by the gmail-mine edge function to auto-classify inbound mail. The table is
-- created (empty) in 0005; a fresh `supabase db reset` therefore had NO sender data and
-- lookup_known_sender() would never match, silently degrading intake routing.
--
-- This seeds the FULL live set: 723 rows (all source='manual'), snapshot 2026-06-20
-- from project dxoikltymmknxqpkpyhi via read-only MCP. id / created_at / verified_at are
-- intentionally NOT seeded so the table defaults (gen_random_uuid(), now()) apply.
--
-- Idempotent: the conflict target is the live UNIQUE INDEX idx_known_senders_unique
-- ON (domain, COALESCE(sender_pattern, '')) (see 0005). Re-running or applying on the
-- live DB leaves existing rows untouched. See docs/MIGRATION_GAP_AUDIT.md (B.5).

ON CONFLICT (domain, COALESCE(sender_pattern, ''::text)) DO NOTHING;
